            {
                "entry_id": "ffc4e0d2-36c6-3bc2-9868-1e530d9cb721",
                "word": "stubby",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "677b9108-ef6c-4e03-b26d-0f8a118fef21",
                        "entry_id": "ffc4e0d2-36c6-3bc2-9868-1e530d9cb721",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "stubbies"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "cc7afab6-f66d-389d-963a-0f254062c3a6",
                        "entry_id": "ffc4e0d2-36c6-3bc2-9868-1e530d9cb721",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A small, squat beer bottle."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Australia",
                            "Canada",
                            "US"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ae9ccf44-1f47-4d98-90ab-85f77a2484b4",
                                "sense_id": "cc7afab6-f66d-389d-963a-0f254062c3a6",
                                "text": "While most stubbies looked alike, there was one distinct stubby brought out by Carling-O′Keefe.[…]The era of the stubby was short, however. Although a superior container, it was not chic enough for the 1980s drinker."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4b51c63a-4190-427e-a7c6-31d3dbb47534",
                                "sense_id": "cc7afab6-f66d-389d-963a-0f254062c3a6",
                                "text": "Annie looked at him a bit surprised and came in, and he realized she carried a bottle of beer with her. Not a stubby, but a long neck."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cb0c4e22-90ff-4814-8f99-8eb71cdf7d2b",
                                "sense_id": "cc7afab6-f66d-389d-963a-0f254062c3a6",
                                "text": "Near the memorial were some wine casks and an unopened stubby of beer, whose label was yet to fade, which had been left to slake the thirst of the deceased."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "72aaedf4-0351-4f89-b73b-790676381af6",
                                "sense_id": "cc7afab6-f66d-389d-963a-0f254062c3a6",
                                "text": "Another notable thing that happens this month is the debut of Spycatcher on Star TV.[…]But come Wednesday night, he sits in the TV room with his stubby of Foster′s beer and watches Steve Nolan catch dirty foreigners (called Commies) selling secrets to some Russian organization called the KGB."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "14dec005-2fb6-4b66-8553-e40db436ce7a",
                                "sense_id": "cc7afab6-f66d-389d-963a-0f254062c3a6",
                                "text": "I had everything planned, and later I kept a stubby behind the spare tire of my ′37 Ford until the bottle was better aged than the beer. I don′t know what happened to it but I′m surprised that it didn′t explode with the heat of that summer."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "250a36a1-476d-4de2-a67a-f3404899403c",
                                "sense_id": "cc7afab6-f66d-389d-963a-0f254062c3a6",
                                "text": "A schooner (425ml in Queensland), when you allow for the collar, is not much more beer than a stubby. A stubby of home brew costs me 25 cents."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2c5f97c8-3a78-40c9-8add-8657381cfeac",
                                "sense_id": "cc7afab6-f66d-389d-963a-0f254062c3a6",
                                "text": "The Liquor Trades Union member concedes that both dogs are quite clever, but says his is even cleverer. His dog, named Measure, is told to go and fetch a stubby of beer and pour seven ounces into a ten-ounce glass. It does this perfectly."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "60d83346-eb27-4c83-b22c-84581109dbe6",
                                "sense_id": "cc7afab6-f66d-389d-963a-0f254062c3a6",
                                "text": "Anyhow, so I goes into the bar and there′s the donkey having a beer with a tourist. See, the way they done it was, they′d hold up the stubby and the donkey would just guzzle it down, like there was no tomorrow."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
